<a id="Using_Custom_Developed_Checkstyle_Checks"></a>

# Custom Developed Checkstyle Checks

This example shows how to create a Maven project for your own Checkstyle checks.
The project builds a JAR file, which you add as a dependency of the Checkstyle Plugin in your other projects.

A [package names file](https://checkstyle.org/config.html#Packages) named `checkstyle_packages.xml` in the JAR lets your Checkstyle configuration refer to the checks by their short names.

This example uses the [example check](https://checkstyle.org/writing-checks.html#Visitor_in_action) from the Checkstyle website.

<a id="Structuring_your_project"></a>

Project Structure
-----------------

This project has the directory structure below:

```text
mycompany-checkstyle-checks
|-- pom.xml
`-- src
    `-- main
        |-- java
        |   `-- com
        |       `-- mycompany
        |           `-- checks
        |               `-- MethodLimitCheck.java
        `-- resources
            `-- checkstyle_packages.xml
```

The sections below describe the three files.

#[[### `pom.xml`]]#

This POM adds a dependency on Checkstyle.
Use the Checkstyle version that the plugin runs; the `provided` scope keeps it out of your JAR's dependencies.

```xml
<project>
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
  <groupId>com.mycompany</groupId>
  <artifactId>mycompany-checkstyle-checks</artifactId>
  <name>MyCompany Checkstyle Checks</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.puppycrawl.tools</groupId>
      <artifactId>checkstyle</artifactId>
      <version>${checkstyleVersion}</version>
      <scope>provided</scope>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>
</project>
```

<a id="packagenames.xml"></a>

#[[### `checkstyle_packages.xml`]]#

Checkstyle reads every `checkstyle_packages.xml` file at the root of the classpath.
This one adds `com.mycompany.checks` to the packages that Checkstyle searches for modules.
You can then use your checks in the Checkstyle configuration without their package name.

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<!DOCTYPE checkstyle-packages PUBLIC
  "-//Checkstyle//DTD Package Names Configuration 1.0//EN"
  "https://checkstyle.org/dtds/packages_1_0.dtd">

<checkstyle-packages>
  <package name="com.mycompany.checks"/>
</checkstyle-packages>
```

#[[### `MethodLimitCheck.java`]]#

Here is the example check from the Checkstyle site.
It checks that a class or interface does not have more than 30 methods.
The `max` property can change the limit.

```java
package com.mycompany.checks;

import com.puppycrawl.tools.checkstyle.api.AbstractCheck;
import com.puppycrawl.tools.checkstyle.api.DetailAST;
import com.puppycrawl.tools.checkstyle.api.TokenTypes;

public class MethodLimitCheck extends AbstractCheck {

    private int max = 30;

    public void setMax(int max) {
        this.max = max;
    }

    @Override
    public int[] getDefaultTokens() {
        return new int[] {TokenTypes.CLASS_DEF, TokenTypes.INTERFACE_DEF};
    }

    @Override
    public int[] getAcceptableTokens() {
        return getDefaultTokens();
    }

    @Override
    public int[] getRequiredTokens() {
        return new int[0];
    }

    @Override
    public void visitToken(DetailAST ast) {
        // find the OBJBLOCK node below the CLASS_DEF/INTERFACE_DEF
        DetailAST objBlock = ast.findFirstToken(TokenTypes.OBJBLOCK);
        // count the number of direct children of the OBJBLOCK that are METHOD_DEFs
        int methodDefs = objBlock.getChildCount(TokenTypes.METHOD_DEF);
        // report a violation if the limit is exceeded
        if (methodDefs > max) {
            log(ast, "too many methods, only " + max + " are allowed");
        }
    }
}
```

<a id="Building_a_JAR_for_your_custom_checks_project"></a>

Build the JAR for Your Custom Checks Project
--------------------------------------------

To use your custom checks in other projects, package and install them:

```shell
mvn install
```

This command builds a JAR file with these contents and installs it into your local repository.

#[[### `mycompany-checkstyle-checks-1.0.jar`]]#

```text
mycompany-checkstyle-checks-1.0.jar
|-- META-INF
|   |-- MANIFEST.MF
|   `-- maven
|       `-- com.mycompany
|           `-- mycompany-checkstyle-checks
|               |-- pom.xml
|               `-- pom.properties
|-- checkstyle_packages.xml
`-- com
    `-- mycompany
        `-- checks
            `-- MethodLimitCheck.class
```

<a id="Using_your_checks_in_another_project"></a>

Use Your Checks in Another Project
----------------------------------

You are now ready to use your custom checks in another project.

#[[### Create a Checkstyle configuration]]#

Create the file `checkstyle.xml` in the root of the project that uses your custom checks.
In this file, tell Checkstyle which checks to run.
Thanks to `checkstyle_packages.xml`, `MethodLimit` is enough; you do not need the fully qualified class name.

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>

<!DOCTYPE module PUBLIC
  "-//Checkstyle//DTD Checkstyle Configuration 1.3//EN"
  "https://checkstyle.org/dtds/configuration_1_3.dtd">

<module name="Checker">
  <module name="TreeWalker">
    <module name="MethodLimit">
      <property name="max" value="20"/>
    </module>
  </module>
</module>
```

#[[### Configure the Checkstyle Plugin to use your custom checks]]#

Finally, tell the other project to use your custom Checkstyle checks.
Add this configuration to the `pom.xml` of that project.

**Note:** Declare the plugin dependency on `mycompany-checkstyle-checks` in the `<build>` section of your `pom.xml`.
The `<reporting>` section does not support plugin dependencies, but the report uses the ones declared in `<build>`.
Do the rest of the configuration in the normal way in the `<reporting>` section.

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-checkstyle-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <dependencies>
          <dependency>
            <groupId>com.mycompany</groupId>
            <artifactId>mycompany-checkstyle-checks</artifactId>
            <version>1.0</version>
          </dependency>
        </dependencies>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-checkstyle-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <configLocation>checkstyle.xml</configLocation>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

Run `mvn site` for the report, or `mvn checkstyle:check -Dcheckstyle.config.location=checkstyle.xml` to check from the command line.
With `max` set to `2`, a class with three methods logs:

```text
[ERROR] src/main/java/com/example/Big.java:[3,1] (extension) MethodLimit: too many methods, only 2 are allowed
```
